<title>CHINA: Hainan Airlines buys 7 Fairchild planes.</title>
<headline>Hainan Airlines buys 7 Fairchild planes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Hainan Airlines Co Ltd plans to buy seven passenger jets worth a total of $30 million from Fairchild Dornier Corp this year, an airline official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The seven 18-seat Metro-23 aircraft would be delivered in the second half of this year, the official said by telephone from Haikou, capital of southern Hainan province.</p>
<p>The planes would be used on short routes between Haikou and nearby cities, he said, without giving further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
